"κυ^νηγ-έτης, ου, ὁ, Dor. (never in Trag.) κυνα—γέτα—ς Pi. N. 6.14 :— huntsman, Od. 9.120 , E. HF 860 (troch.), Hec. 1174 , Pl. R. 432b , X. Cyn. 6.11 , al., OGI 20 (iii B.C.); in pl. of certain δαίμονες, Pl.Com. 174.16 , SIG 1040.9 (Piraeus, iv B.C.): metaph., of one who seeks fame, Pi.l.c.:—fem. κυ^νηγ-έτις, Dor. κυ^νηγ-α—γέτις, ιδος, huntress, Ach.Tat. 8.12 ; epith. of Artemis, Corn. ND 34 : as Adj., κ. αἰγανέα AP 6.115 (Antip.)."